{
  "title": "CHAPTER 16  INDIAN NATIONAL MOVEMENT (1857–1947)-CONTINUATION",
  "order": 3,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "wkxl5cl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. LUCKNOW PACT (1916)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Lucknow Pact (1916) established unity between the INC and Muslim League through separate electorates.",
        "The all-British Simon Commission (1927) was met with nationwide boycotts and the slogan 'Simon Go Back'.",
        "The Lahore Session (1929) declared Purna Swaraj (Complete Independence), fixing 26 January 1930 as the milestone date.",
        "The Poona Pact (1932) between Gandhi and Dr. B.R. Ambedkar replaced separate electorates with reserved seats.",
        "The Mountbatten Plan (1947) formulated partition and enabled the Indian Independence Act 1947."
      ],
      "id": "qnfcjq7"
    },
